40,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out the current spot is a real hotspot for complaints, and the frontages aren't all the same size. Some of us have much less space to work with than others.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I found that supervising the bins on the next lane takes about fifty minutes, and the station block's bin house actually smells worse in the summer than an open pile.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The ward can refund forty percent of a shelter, but they're pretty expensive! Also, we've been spending thirty-four thousand yen a year just on nets and deodorants for the open bags.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I learned that people at the residents' meeting are hesitant to be the ""bad guy"" and turn away late bags, and the station block ended up arguing over maintenance costs.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The truck arrives quite early, between seven forty and eight fifteen, and the clerk informed me that any permanent build requires a measured plan and four months for approval.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if the bin house smells worse, maybe a permanent structure isn't the answer. And since the frontages vary, we can't just assume any spot works for everyone.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree, @May. If a structure just traps the smell and the space is limited, we might be trading one problem for another. We need something that doesn't create a new nuisance.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, if we're already spending thirty-four thousand yen a year on nets and smells, maybe a shelter would actually save us money in the long run? Or would it just be more expensive?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, the station block's minutes showed they fought over who pays for repairs. Even if it saves on nets, we might just start arguing about broken latches instead.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we must be cautious. A permanent structure requires significant time for approval and may lead to future disputes over maintenance, which would be a heavy burden on our spirits.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, you're right about the burden. Plus, the complaint log shows the person currently hosting the bins is exhausted. We can't just leave it where it is without a real change.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we can't build something and we can't leave it as is, maybe we should look at how we manage the time. But @Servas, that truck arrival time is quite early, isn't it?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"It is! If we have to be there before eight, that's going to be tough for some of us. But maybe we can rotate who has to wake up early?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, rotating the duty sounds fair, but we must remember that some people find it hard to be the one enforcing the rules on their neighbors.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Servas,,"That is a profound point, Midori. We must ensure that our solution does not turn neighbors into police officers, for the peace of the heart is more valuable than the tidiness of the street.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,May,,"Exactly. If we rotate the location, we solve the complaint issue, but we have to make sure the narrowest frontages can actually handle the bins without blocking the path.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"If we rotate, we avoid the smell of a bin house and the stress of policing, but we must be realistic about the space @May mentioned. Let's see what the actual options are.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready to see the options! I hope there's one that's cheap and doesn't make anyone too grumpy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Let's look for a solution that balances the physical space and the financial cost while keeping our friendships intact.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Servas,,I believe we have gathered sufficient wisdom to weigh our choices. Let us now examine the paths available to us and choose the one that fosters the most harmony.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
